    num: '04',
    title: 'Assuming "wanting to help" protects you from burnout',
    body: 'Research on compassion fatigue found empathy itself is a risk factor, not a shield - some nursing subgroups showed 82-86% experiencing moderate to high compassion fatigue or burnout. Wanting to help is the reason people enter these fields. It is not the reason they last in them.',
