    Once you pick a track, the feeling of wanting to help stops mattering and something else takes over: visible proof that you can actually do the work, not just feel called to it. This looks different across each track, but the underlying logic is the same everywhere - one finished, checkable piece of work beats a stated love of helping people. <strong>This is also the actual mechanism behind higher pay</strong>: the right track plus one visible proof asset is what turns a motivation into a high-value skill portfolio, not the motivation by itself.
